<title>USA: Hyundai Motor increases incentives.</title>
<headline>Hyundai Motor increases incentives.</headline>
<dateline>FOUNTAIN VALLEY, Calif. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hyundai Motor America, a unit of Hyundai Motor Co Ltd, said Tuesday it increased incentives by $500 on the 1996 Elantra sedan and the 1997 Elantra and Sonata sedans.</p>
<p>These incentives, as well as those on other models, will run through March 31.</p>
<p>Hyundai said the increase brings 1996 Elantra sedan incentives to $1,500 and Sonata to $2,000. On 1997 models, the incentives now are $500 on the Accent, $500 on Tiburon, $1,000 on Sonata and $1,000 on Elantra.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
